<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10400" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίπορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίπορθμος</span>
			, <i>on the opposite coast,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ἀ. γείτονα χώραν,</span> i.e.
			Europe, as separated by a strait from Asia, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				66
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				544
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				210
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρτεμιν Χαλκίδος
			ἀντίπορον,</span> i.e. her templeat Aulis <i>over against</i>
			Chalcis in Euboea, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IA</u>
				1494
			</span></i> (all lyr. passages): —in <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.2.18
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἀ. λόφον τῷ μαστῷ,</span>
			simply, <i>over against, opposite to.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
